372
00:52:47.240 --> 00:52:57.370
Edward Wertz (Hashgraph): The connector to use to pay for the remote execution, the target application on the remote ledger, and the data payload that it wants to send to that remote ledger.

373
00:52:57.940 --> 00:53:02.800
Edward Wertz (Hashgraph): The Clipper service then asks locally, the connector.

374
00:53:03.290 --> 00:53:10.490
Edward Wertz (Hashgraph): Given all this data, are you willing to subsidize the execution of the transaction of this message on the remote ledger?

375
00:53:10.760 --> 00:53:14.079
Edward Wertz (Hashgraph): The connector has the ability to say yes or no.

376
00:53:14.200 --> 00:53:28.059
Edward Wertz (Hashgraph): If it says no, the attempt to send the message is rejected and handed back to the application. If it says yes, the Clipper service then enqueues the message bundle. Message data on the outgoing message queue. The…

